2026-05-27 14:42:23,098 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent received: The client demands a high level of security, with particular attention to the protection of personal data (GDPR compliance) and sovereignty of data (SecNumCloud-type infrastructure). How can we ensure our solution meets these security requirements, and what measures do we need to take to guarantee the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of the data?
2026-05-27 14:43:38,094 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-05-27 14:43:38,094 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: To meet the client's demands for a high level of security, particularly regarding GDPR compliance and data sovereignty in line with SecNumCloud standards, we must leverage our existing ISO 27001 certification, which covers the design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems. This certification ensures that our information security management system is robust and capable of protecting sensitive data.

For GDPR compliance, we have a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed, and their contact information is dpo@nexus-engineering.it. We also have experience with conducting Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs), which typically take about 3 weeks to complete. Our standard data residency policy ensures that all data is stored within the EU, aligning with GDPR requirements for data localization.

To address cross-border transfer concerns, our policy prohibits such transfers by default unless there's an explicit legal basis for doing so. We utilize anonymization tools like Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom Named Entity Recognition (NER) models to protect personal data. Additionally, we have implemented mechanisms for data subjects to exercise their rights, including access, rectification, erasure, portability, and objection.

For ensuring the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data, especially in a SecNumCloud context, we rely on our experience with risk management as outlined in ISO 27005. We also have specific measures in place such as multi-factor authentication (MFA) using TOTP or hardware tokens (FIDO2), role-based access control (RBAC) design, and privileged access management solutions like CyberArk Conjur and HashiCorp Vault.

Our network security architecture is based on zero-trust principles, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth strategies. We have intrusion detection and prevention systems deployed and conduct regular penetration testing - at least annually and post-major releases, with the last test conducted on September 15, 2024, resulting in two medium findings that were remediated.

Given our experience with ANSSI's SecNumCloud projects (three projects) and RGS v2, we are well-positioned to meet the client's requirements for data sovereignty and security. We also have real-time SIEM integration capabilities using tools like Wazuh and Elastic SIEM, ensuring prompt detection of security incidents.

To further guarantee the security and compliance of our solution, we must ensure that all AI models used are secured against prompt injection attacks, with output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, and confidence threshold escalation in place. Model updates will undergo thorough security reviews.

