2026-05-27 14:49:07,825 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: # 1. Executive Summary
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with its specialized agents, proposes a comprehensive artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents of the City of Belval in their daily administrative tasks. Our solution integrates AI-powered information search, drafting support, file analysis, and suggestion of actions, ensuring compliance with GDPR, EU AI Act, and other regulatory requirements. Leveraging our expertise in cloud integration, security, and sustainability, we aim to improve the efficiency and quality of service rendered by municipal agents while minimizing environmental impact.

# 2. Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval seeks an artificial intelligence solution that assists its agents in accessing information, drafting administrative contents, analyzing files, and suggesting actions within a secure, GDPR-compliant, and environmentally sustainable framework. The solution must integrate with existing systems, provide explainable recommendations, and ensure data sovereignty through hosting on EU-based infrastructures like SecNumCloud.

# 3. Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution utilizes a large language model (LLM) such as Mistral 7B or LLaMA 3 8B, fine-tuned for the specific needs of municipal agents in Belval. This AI core will be integrated with knowledge graphs for procedural reasoning and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities to enhance information retrieval and generation accuracy. For security and compliance, we leverage our ISO 27001 certification, ensuring a robust information security management system. Data will be hosted exclusively on Outscale (SecNumCloud), an EU-certified infrastructure, with no data transfers outside the EU. Sensitive data will be protected through anonymization tools like Microsoft Presidio and custom Named Entity Recognition (NER) models.

To meet performance requirements, our Technical Architect Agent proposes a hybrid deployment with auto-scaling capabilities on Outscale, utilizing containerization via Docker and Kubernetes, and infrastructure as code (IAC) tools like Terraform. Monitoring will be conducted using Prometheus and Grafana to ensure response times below 2 seconds and availability above 99.9%. Security design patterns include zero-trust network architecture, encryption, and secrets management with HashiCorp Vault.

Our Legal Agent ensures compliance with GDPR and the EU AI Act, emphasizing transparency and explainability in AI recommendations. No automated decisions will be made without explicit validation by a municipal agent. We have a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed and conduct regular Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs).

The Budget Agent confirms our financial eligibility to bid, with a maximum contract value of 3 million euros over 4 years. Assuming an even distribution of costs, our projected annual margin could be approximately 210,000 euros, based on a target gross margin percentage of 28%. However, this calculation does not account for specific project costs or potential discounts and will require detailed costing and negotiations with the client.

For sustainability, we partner with green hosting providers like OVHcloud or Scaleway, utilizing 100% renewable energy and efficient data centers (PUE ratings of 1.3 and 1.28). Digital sobriety practices include INT8/INT4 model quantisation to reduce GPU energy consumption by approximately 40%, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching to reduce recomputes by an estimated 20%, and adhering to a green IT hardware procurement policy.

# 4. Unaddressed Requirements
No specific requirements from the tender are left unaddressed in our proposal, as we have covered technical architecture, security compliance, legal eligibility, budgetary considerations, AI innovation, and CSR sustainability aspects.

# 5. Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., through its consortium of specialized agents, offers a comprehensive and integrated solution that meets the City of Belval's requirements for an artificial intelligence-powered assistance tool. Our proposal ensures GDPR compliance, high security standards, explainable AI recommendations, efficient performance, and environmental sustainability. We believe our solution will significantly enhance the efficiency and quality of service provided by municipal agents, aligning with the city's digital transformation strategy while respecting its budgetary and environmental commitments.
